# Source Page Template

Source pages document the origin of information and link to raw materials.

## Frontmatter

```yaml
---
type: source
title: "Title of the Source Document"
source_type: paper | article | book | video | dataset
url: "https://example.com/original-source"
raw_path: "raw/papers/filename.pdf"
date_published: YYYY-MM-DD
date_added: YYYY-MM-DD
author: "Author Name"
publisher: "Publication Name"
tags: [tag1, tag2, tag3]
status: processed | pending | archived
---
```

## Body Structure

```markdown
# Title of the Source Document

## Summary

Brief overview of the source content (2-4 sentences).

## Key Claims

1. First major claim from this source
2. Second important claim
3. Third key finding

## Entities Mentioned

- [[entity-001|Person Name]] - Description of their role
- [[entity-002|Organization]] - What they do
- [[entity-003|Location]] - Relevance to source

## Concepts Discussed

- [[concept-001|Concept Name]] - How it's used here
- [[concept-002|Another Concept]] - Brief explanation

## Key Quotes

> "Important verbatim quote from the source" (p. 42)

## Notes

Additional observations, context, or agent interpretations.
```

